1
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:15,724
JE GEUN-U
HAN YEONG-HUI

2
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:19,060
<i>When I was in high school,</i>

3
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:22,480
<i>my mother drove into the ocean</i>
<i>with my father in the car.</i>

4
00:00:25,191 --> 00:00:27,110
<i>My mom made it out of the water,</i>

5
00:00:27,902 --> 00:00:29,029
<i>but my poor father</i>

6
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:33,491
<i>is probably still wandering alone</i>
<i>somewhere in the deep ocean.</i>

7
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:38,621
<i>The fingernails my crazy mom left me.</i>

8
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:43,334
<i>That's when I knew it wasn't an accident.</i>

9
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:46,379
- Don't you think it was insurance fraud?
- That's what I'm saying.

10
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:49,924
<i>It was both suicide and murder,</i>

11
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:51,926
<i>but I said nothing.</i>

12
00:00:52,761 --> 00:00:54,596
<i>I was still too young</i>

13
00:00:55,263 --> 00:00:56,723
<i>to bear all of it.</i>

14
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:00,602
<i>How could I have ever lived a normal life?</i>

15
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:04,606
<i>A severe panic disorder.</i>

16
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:08,735
<i>From that day on, I couldn't go outside</i>
<i>without my medication.</i>

17
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:11,821
<i>But even with it,</i>
<i>I still wouldn't go outside.</i>

18
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:14,908
<i>A happy and peaceful confinement.</i>

19
00:01:16,284 --> 00:01:19,412
<i>Maybe that's when people started</i>

20
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:24,042
<i>to see me as a rat hiding in a hole.</i>

21
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:32,926
<i>This is the Hangang River area</i>

22
00:01:33,009 --> 00:01:35,595
<i>where a woman in her early thirties</i>
<i>was found dead.</i>

23
00:01:35,678 --> 00:01:37,430
<i>Authorities are identifying the woman,</i>

24
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:41,810
<i>but they were unable to find any leads,</i>
<i>including family or acquaintances.</i>

25
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:44,813
<i>The entire area</i>
<i>was temporarily closed off…</i>

26
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:46,272
<i>I</i>

27
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:49,192
<i>still can't go outside.</i>

28
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:55,448
<i>The world goes on just fine without me.</i>

29
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,451
<i>For the past three years,</i>

30
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:01,496
<i>while I've been trapped in this house,</i>

31
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:05,333
<i>the world has been just as lively as ever,</i>

32
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:07,752
<i>every single day.</i>

33
00:02:11,422 --> 00:02:12,757
<i>Damn it.</i>

34
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:15,927
<i>It just won't fall apart.</i>

35
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:22,392
<i>While I'm stuck here,</i>
<i>popping pills for my panic disorder.</i>

36
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:35,113
YOUR ORDER IS PLACED!
ARRIVING TOMORROW MORNING (SAT)

37
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:14,629
<i>People go around</i>
<i>calling me a genius writer.</i>

38
00:04:15,129 --> 00:04:19,676
<i>A reclusive writer shrouded in mystery,</i>
<i>known only by a pen name,</i>

39
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:22,428
<i>with neither a face nor a real name.</i>

40
00:04:28,726 --> 00:04:33,106
<i>A mysterious new writer</i>
<i>who burst onto the scene like a comet,</i>

41
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:35,316
<i>releasing one hit novel after another.</i>

42
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:44,284
<i>A comet?</i>

43
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:49,539
<i>At least comets</i>
<i>can roam through space freely.</i>

44
00:05:03,594 --> 00:05:05,054
<i>Fuck.</i>

45
00:05:06,848 --> 00:05:08,474
<i>They know nothing.</i>

46
00:05:33,624 --> 00:05:35,376
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

47
00:05:38,921 --> 00:05:41,215
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

48
00:05:44,218 --> 00:05:46,387
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

49
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,685
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

50
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:07,367
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

51
00:06:10,161 --> 00:06:11,496
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

52
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:18,461
<i>The same nightmare every night.</i>

53
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:21,881
<i>The same panic attack every day.</i>

54
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:26,052
<i>Nothing ever changes.</i>

55
00:07:10,054 --> 00:07:11,681
<i>Let's see</i>

56
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:15,268
<i>if anything has changed since yesterday.</i>

57
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:18,104
<i>Yakult.</i>

58
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:22,150
<i>The mailman. Saying hello.</i>

59
00:07:24,068 --> 00:07:25,236
<i>I'm here at the scene in…</i>

60
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:26,988
<i>The same news.</i>

61
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:30,032
<i>Maybe the outside world</i>

62
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:32,785
<i>really is a simulation.</i>

63
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:35,788
<i>…where a woman was found dead yesterday.</i>

64
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:39,500
<i>This is usually a quiet neighborhood, but…</i>

65
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,043
<i>I'm so sick of it all.</i>

66
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:43,796
<i>…and investigators flooded the area,</i>

67
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:47,049
<i>tensions remained high for some time.</i>

68
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:51,179
<i>The victim was found</i>
<i>with severe external injuries.</i>

69
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:55,558
<i>Police have secured CCTV footage</i>
<i>of a suspect leaving the scene</i>

70
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:58,686
<i>and are working</i>
<i>to identify and track the individual.</i>

71
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:10,198
BARO BANK

72
00:08:13,868 --> 00:08:15,244
BARO BANK CERTIFICATE

73
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:16,871
Huh?

74
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,752
FINGERPRINT NOT MATCHED

75
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:25,713
What the hell?

76
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:32,428
FINGERPRINT NOT MATCHED

77
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:34,597
TOO MANY FAILED ATTEMPTS
ENTER YOUR PIN

78
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:50,404
What was that?

79
00:08:58,871 --> 00:09:00,122
Is this a bug?

80
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:13,511
DONGBU POLICE STATION

81
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:17,932
You're here.

82
00:09:18,015 --> 00:09:19,141
Where have you been?

83
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:20,977
The courthouse?

84
00:09:22,186 --> 00:09:23,646
Is that still going on?

85
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:28,067
Hey. Get to work.

86
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:30,111
I'm working. Covering your part too.

87
00:09:30,194 --> 00:09:32,363
Fuck, we're already short-handed as hell.

88
00:09:37,743 --> 00:09:39,495
- Morning, sir.
- Hey.

89
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:40,580
Sir.

90
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:42,164
You little punk.

91
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:44,917
Where have you been? The courthouse?

92
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:49,046
At least tell me where you're going
before you disappear, punk!

93
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:52,008
A freaking cop, going in and out
of domestic violence court?

94
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:54,969
It wasn't violence.

95
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:58,389
All I did was punch the wall once.

96
00:09:58,472 --> 00:10:01,142
That's violence, punk. Against the wall.

97
00:10:01,225 --> 00:10:02,852
Yeah, nice going.

98
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:04,687
Hey.

99
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:08,899
Just get to work.

100
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:10,151
You get to work.

101
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:11,652
Gonna work or what, punks?

102
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:21,329
Hey, you.

103
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:24,040
Looks like you got a tip.

104
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:26,876
A tip?

105
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:29,712
Yeah. Might be about the body found
in the Hangang River.

106
00:10:29,795 --> 00:10:30,630
But why you?

107
00:10:31,213 --> 00:10:32,506
Is it someone you know?

108
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:34,884
Who sent it?

109
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:36,260
It's anonymous.

110
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:38,262
Then why ask if I knew them?

111
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:40,306
I was talking about the bastard in there.

112
00:10:40,389 --> 00:10:42,266
Oh, someone's in here?

113
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:44,268
Huh? Jesus.

114
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:51,400
THE BODY FOUND IN THE HANGANG RIVER
WAS NOT A SUICIDE

115
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:58,115
KIM YEONG-GEUN
APT 704, BLDG 104, CENTUM HEIGHTS FORE

116
00:11:02,411 --> 00:11:03,454
You know that guy?

117
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:04,997
No. Never seen him before.

118
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,000
There must be a reason this came to you.

119
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:12,421
Who mails stuff like this these days?
They'd just post it online.

120
00:11:13,547 --> 00:11:15,758
So who killed themselves
in the Hangang River?

121
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:17,843
How would I know, punk?

122
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:20,680
Yeah, you find out. It was sent to you.

123
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:22,473
- Take care, sir.
- Where are you going?

124
00:11:22,556 --> 00:11:24,183
- Who is this?
- Seriously!

125
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:26,894
How the hell would I find out? Seriously…

126
00:11:26,977 --> 00:11:28,562
- Hey, kid.
- Sir?

127
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:30,773
Run a background check.

128
00:11:31,273 --> 00:11:33,651
Name, Kim Yeong-geun. ID number…

129
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:37,029
Find out.

130
00:11:39,323 --> 00:11:40,366
Yes, sir.

131
00:11:57,675 --> 00:11:59,176
TO SON SOO-HYUN

132
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:02,763
APT 704, BLDG 104
CENTUM HEIGHTS FORE

133
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:22,324
You call me over way too often
just because I'm nearby.

134
00:12:22,908 --> 00:12:25,202
You know, you sure use a lot of gas.

135
00:12:25,911 --> 00:12:27,329
You got a cold or something?

136
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:30,124
How would I catch a cold?

137
00:12:30,207 --> 00:12:32,334
I never go outside.

138
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:34,378
Unless you give it to me.

139
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:39,383
Hey.

140
00:12:40,634 --> 00:12:41,719
What's that?

141
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:44,847
It's a bug.

142
00:12:44,930 --> 00:12:46,307
A bug.

143
00:12:57,067 --> 00:12:58,486
I saved my number in there.

144
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:00,654
You don't have anyone else to call anyway.

145
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:04,408
But this thing was working perfectly fine,
wasn't it?

146
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:07,077
You watched porn?

147
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:08,871
Shut up.

148
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:12,917
Then why is it acting up all of a sudden?

149
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,419
I know. The fingerprint isn't working,

150
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:17,505
so I can't make payments or anything.

151
00:13:17,588 --> 00:13:20,424
You got it for me a few months ago.
Why does it keep acting up?

152
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:22,760
Hey, show me your fingers.

153
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:26,722
Maybe you wrote so much,
your fingerprints wore off.

154
00:13:27,681 --> 00:13:29,600
Having fun? Huh?

155
00:13:32,102 --> 00:13:32,937
Hey.

156
00:13:33,437 --> 00:13:35,856
If it's urgent,
I can pay for it for you now.

157
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,566
Everything in the cart, right?

158
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:38,484
Yeah.

159
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:40,861
Oh, and the OTP is in there,

160
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:43,364
so just set up your fingerprint
in the banking app.

161
00:13:43,447 --> 00:13:45,699
Man, you really are a handful.

162
00:13:45,783 --> 00:13:46,909
You got a better idea?

163
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:49,954
The accounts are all in your name,
and all the money's with you.

164
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:52,998
Your money's safe, so don't worry.

165
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:54,291
Anything else?

166
00:13:54,834 --> 00:13:55,918
That.

167
00:13:56,544 --> 00:13:58,546
I'll call someone to take care of it.

168
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:04,718
Every day's been the same for me.

169
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:06,804
Why's all this happening today?

170
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:07,805
Oh man.

171
00:14:07,888 --> 00:14:08,722
Who knows?

172
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:11,725
Maybe the phone and the glass
were all part of the plan.

173
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:17,314
Isn't that the simulation theory?
The story you wrote.

174
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:22,695
Hey, the protagonist
was manipulated into believing that.

175
00:14:22,778 --> 00:14:23,946
Did you actually read it?

176
00:14:24,029 --> 00:14:25,823
I bought it, punk. Isn't that enough?

177
00:14:25,906 --> 00:14:28,951
You expect me to actually read
the whole thing too?

178
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:30,619
What about your meds?

179
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:32,830
- Do you have enough?
- Yeah, I've still got some.

180
00:14:33,497 --> 00:14:35,291
All right, then.

181
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:39,795
Thanks to you,
I've gotta play a panic disorder patient.

182
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:41,255
I'm getting good at acting.

183
00:14:41,338 --> 00:14:42,715
Was that all?

184
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:45,676
Yeah. You're leaving already?

185
00:14:45,759 --> 00:14:47,845
Accountants don't just sit around all day.

186
00:14:48,345 --> 00:14:50,222
There's our school reunion today too.

187
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:51,515
I'm busy as hell.

188
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:53,058
You guys still get together?

189
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:54,643
You're the only one not coming.

190
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:56,812
All the guys who made a bit of money
show up.

191
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:59,607
Man, that shitty high school.

192
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:02,276
Reunion, my ass.
Aren't you sick of it already?

193
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:06,405
And you aren't sick of being stuck here?
It's been three years already.

194
00:15:06,488 --> 00:15:07,698
I mean, besides me,

195
00:15:08,198 --> 00:15:09,575
nobody else comes to see you.

196
00:15:10,618 --> 00:15:12,119
Of course I'm sick of it.

197
00:15:14,079 --> 00:15:16,332
You said you'd get me out of here. When?

198
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:18,459
Yeah, you will.

199
00:15:19,418 --> 00:15:23,422
You'll feel better once you're somewhere
with beaches, palm trees, and all that.

200
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:29,386
Just wait. I'll get you out of here soon.

201
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:32,973
Bye now.

202
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:37,436
- When are you coming back?
- Call me if anything happens.

203
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:39,355
I'll come right away.

204
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:41,774
Hey.

205
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:23,816
BARO BANK CERTIFICATE
FINGERPRINT NOT MATCHED

206
00:16:32,199 --> 00:16:33,993
What the hell is wrong with this again?

207
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:36,764
Who is it?

208
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:38,932
<i>Oh, yes. I'm with the police.</i>

209
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:48,233
What brings you here?

210
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:51,236
Well, we've got a report.
Mr. Kim Yeong-geun?

211
00:17:52,696 --> 00:17:53,989
No.

212
00:17:54,073 --> 00:17:55,657
- You're not?
- No, I'm not.

213
00:17:57,034 --> 00:17:58,160
Doesn't he live here?

214
00:17:58,994 --> 00:18:01,622
No. No one by that name does.

215
00:18:01,705 --> 00:18:03,457
Damn.

216
00:18:04,249 --> 00:18:05,959
We've got a report, and…

217
00:18:06,752 --> 00:18:08,504
Can I take a quick look around?

218
00:18:11,673 --> 00:18:13,300
- Sure. Go ahead.
- All right.

219
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:15,135
This won't take long.

220
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:19,640
Oh wow.

221
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:21,725
This place is huge.

222
00:18:24,103 --> 00:18:25,938
Oh, a bird flew into it.

223
00:18:27,856 --> 00:18:28,982
A bird?

224
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:32,027
There are still birds
flying into these things, huh?

225
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,071
Strange.

226
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:35,948
That must've hurt.

227
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:39,701
Do you live alone?

228
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:40,619
Yes.

229
00:18:46,750 --> 00:18:49,795
Wow, this is a really nice place.

230
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:56,510
If you've confirmed they're not here,

231
00:18:56,593 --> 00:18:58,303
please leave now.

232
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:01,807
Sure, I was gonna leave anyway.

233
00:19:13,485 --> 00:19:15,487
It said Kim Yeong-geun lives here.

234
00:19:15,571 --> 00:19:17,239
Who's that person anyway?

235
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:18,532
No idea.

236
00:19:18,615 --> 00:19:21,076
Who knows? He might be hiding here.

237
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:37,968
Fine, then. Look.

238
00:19:39,636 --> 00:19:41,722
Thank you for your cooperation.

239
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,025
Are you done?

240
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:55,277
Please leave now.

241
00:20:05,996 --> 00:20:08,248
Sure, sorry to bother you.

242
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:15,172
By the way,

243
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:18,300
what do you do?

244
00:20:23,263 --> 00:20:25,390
Yeah, the tip was just a prank.

245
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:27,476
Kim Yeong-geun doesn't even live there.

246
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:30,270
What did he say again?
Just some writer lives there.

247
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:32,189
<i>Did you identify the deceased?</i>

248
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:34,608
How am I supposed to?
They're unidentified.

249
00:20:34,691 --> 00:20:35,567
Who's that thug?

250
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:37,319
<i>How the fuck should I know?</i>

251
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:39,112
We don't even know where he lives.

252
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:40,030
<i>Just with a photo?</i>

253
